 result←object(State ∆Brush)arg;style;color;size;brush;next;thisbrush
 ⍝ Create and return a Brush "handle", which itself contains the properties used for creating brush-based objects
 ⍝ This handle should be "freed" later with '#' ∆WI '⎕Free'

 ⍝ '?Brush' style [fgcolor]
 ⍝ '?Brush' ¯2 bitmap

 thisbrush←(_brush:⍬ ⋄ _color_:State._color_) ⍝ A place to hold the parsed input
 {}object(thisbrush Brush)arg ⍝ Call the standard brush-parsing routine to fill in the normalized parameters

 :If ¯1=⊃thisbrush._brush ⍝ If they just gave us an old handle
     result←2⊃thisbrush._brush ⍝ Just return it as-is and do nothing
 :Else
     ⍝ Build a "handle" namespace out of this definition for later reference; all it needs is the final property-list
     result←'Brush'CreateHandle(Props:DefineBrush thisbrush) ⍝ Turn it into a property-list for creation and store that creation vector
 :EndIf
